# Quick Reference Guide for {{project.name}}

> How to discover and use Qoder rules in your project

## 🎯 What Are These Rules?

The `.qoder/rules/` directory contains AI coding guidelines that help Qoder understand your project standards.

**How Rules Work:**
- Rules are plain markdown files with coding guidelines
- Configure activation in Qoder IDE (right-click file → settings)
- **Apply Manually** - Activate via Qoder UI when needed
- **Model Decision** - Let AI decide when to apply
- **Always Apply** - Active for all interactions (use sparingly!)
- **Specific Files** - Apply based on file patterns

**Character Limit:** Qoder loads up to 100,000 characters across all active rules. If you exceed this, content will be truncated. Use "Apply Manually" for most rules to stay within limits.

For more info, see [Qoder Rules Documentation](https://docs.qoder.com/user-guide/rules).

