## 🎯 Best Practices

### 1. Start with "Apply Manually" for Most Rules

To stay within the 100,000 character limit, use "Apply Manually" as the default. Only set "Always Apply" for critical rules like:
- requirements-spec.md (Quest Mode enforcement)
- security.md (if building APIs/user-facing features)

### 2. Use "Model Decision" for Context-Specific Rules

Let Qoder decide when to apply:
- testing.md (when writing tests)
- api-design.md (when working on API endpoints)
- error-handling.md (when handling errors)

### 3. Combine Multiple Rules for Complex Tasks

Qoder can reference multiple rules simultaneously. For complex features:
- Core standards (requirements-spec.md, core.md)
- Specific domain (api-design.md, security.md)
- Quality checks (testing.md, error-handling.md)

### 4. Review Active Rules Regularly

Check Settings → Rules to see which rules are active and their total character count.

